Title: The Lighthouse Robot
Author: Test Author
Draft date: 2026-01-01
Notes: A made-up script for tests. Every voice is a narrator or a character.

===

INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S ROOM - DAY

MARA winds a brass clock, humming to herself.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Long ago there was a keeper named Mara.

A small ROBOT rolls in carrying a tray of tea and bumps into the table.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
and she had a robot.

OLD SAILOR
"Let there be tea!"

NARRATOR (V.O.)
The robot made tea so well that it could almost whistle.

MARA
"Whistle!"

ROBOT
"Beep boop!"

INT. LIGHTHOUSE STAIRCASE - DAY

MARA is teaching the robot to climb the stairs one step at a time.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
One day, while they were practising, the lamp went dark.

ROBOT spins on the landing and rolls up the stairs towards the lamp room.

MARA
“Wait, what is wrong?”

NARRATOR (V.O.)
said Mara.

CUT TO:

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE BALCONY - DAY

WIDE SHOT of the SEA. MARA steps out and sees the robot holding a glowing lantern over the waves.

MARA
“Oh,”

NARRATOR (V.O.)
she said,

MARA (CONT'D)
“you only wanted to light the lamp.”

[[Check the weather in this scene.]]

The SUN sinks quickly and the MOON climbs the sky.

MARA
"Time for bed."

INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S ROOM - NIGHT

MARA
"Good night,"

ROBOT
“Good night”,

NARRATOR (V.O.)
said the robot.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S ROOM - MORNING

MARA stretches and sits up, then waves the robot towards the harbour. ROBOT rolls out the door.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In the morning Mara asked the robot to fetch the newspaper from the harbour.

She waits for a few minutes, but nothing happens.

CUT TO:

EXT. HARBOUR - MORNING

EXTREME WIDE SHOT of the HARBOUR. A fog bank rolls in and hides the boats.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Then the fog came in and the robot was lost.

CUT TO:

INT. LIGHTHOUSE STAIRCASE - MORNING

CLOSE UP of the LAMP. It flickers once and goes out.

MARA (CONT'D)
"Come back soon."

WIDE SHOT of the staircase. MARA hurries down the steps with a lantern.

CUT TO:

ANOTHER ANGLE of the harbour. The robot rolls out of the fog with the newspaper held high.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
So the robot came home.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Then Mara said,

CLOSE UP of MARA smiling.

MARA
“Thank you, my friend.”

WIDE SHOT of the lighthouse. The lamp comes on and sweeps its beam across the sea.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And the lighthouse shone all night.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
theend
